    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d760">

                <pb facs="0857" n="771" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg771"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-09-01"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that the United States war ships started for Beirut upon the
                    receipt of news of the assassination of the United States viceconsul, and can
                    not now be stopped; that they will be at Beirut the <pb facs="0858" n="772"
                        xml:id="pg772"/> last of the present week. He asks if Mr. Leishman can not
                    have all pending questions settled before their arrival, and states that he has
                    urged this on the Turkish minister in Washington.</p>
                <p>Should the indicated arrangement be made, the war ships will make a brief visit
                    and depart whenever Mr. Leishman says they are no longer needed.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
